{"title":"Career Roadmap · Rehabilitation Therapist","role":"Rehabilitation Therapist","summary":"A Rehabilitation Therapist helps individuals improve or regain functional abilities affected by injury, illness, disability, developmental conditions, neurological disorders, or age-related limitations.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Occupational Therapy (BOT)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Rehabilitation Therapist helps individuals improve or regain functional abilities affected by injury, illness, disability, developmental conditions, neurological disorders, or age-related limitations."},{"type":"p","text":"For the row provided, the most direct pathway is Bachelor of Occupational Therapy (BOT) → Rehabilitation Therapist, particularly when the role focuses on occupational therapy, functional independence, activities of daily living, adaptive techniques, and participation in home, education, and work environments."},{"type":"p","text":"Occupational therapy can involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Activities of daily living training"},{"text":"Upper-limb rehabilitation"},{"text":"Neurological rehabilitation"},{"text":"Pediatric rehabilitation"},{"text":"Cognitive rehabilitation"},{"text":"Assistive devices"},{"text":"Adaptive equipment"},{"text":"Home modification"},{"text":"Vocational rehabilitation"},{"text":"Patient and caregiver education"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"“Rehabilitation Therapist” is a broad job title. Exact scope and eligibility depend on the employer and applicable professional-registration rules. A BOT graduate should practice within the recognized scope of occupational therapy and applicable regulations rather than assuming that all rehabilitation procedures belong to occupational therapy."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"BOT + anatomy + physiology + OT foundations + supervised clinical rotations"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Occupational Therapist / Rehabilitation Therapist → independent caseload management"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior Occupational Therapist → specialized rehabilitation practice"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Clinical Specialist / Rehabilitation Coordinator / OT Department Leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During BOT","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Biomedical & Occupational Therapy Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Basic pathology"},{"text":"Human development"},{"text":"Fundamentals of occupational therapy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop foundational skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Professional ethics"},{"text":"Basic clinical safety"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Key concept"},{"type":"p","text":"Occupational therapy focuses on helping people participate in meaningful activities."},{"type":"p","text":"Think in terms of:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Health Condition","Impairment","Functional Limitation","Difficulty in Daily Activities","Occupational Therapy Assessment","Intervention","Improved Function / Participation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — OT Assessment & Therapeutic Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"h","text":"Musculoskeletal conditions"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fractures"},{"text":"Arthritis"},{"text":"Joint disorders"},{"text":"Tendon injuries"},{"text":"Hand injuries"},{"text":"Post-operative conditions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neurological conditions"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stroke"},{"text":"Traumatic brain injury"},{"text":"Spinal cord injury"},{"text":"Parkinson's disease"},{"text":"Multiple sclerosis"},{"text":"Peripheral nerve disorders"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Developmental conditions"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental delay"},{"text":"Autism spectrum conditions"},{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Learning difficulties"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motor function"},{"text":"Sensory function"},{"text":"Coordination"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Strength"},{"text":"Range of motion"},{"text":"Fine motor skills"},{"text":"Gross motor skills"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Clinical Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical skills in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Functional assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"Assess:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Activities of daily living"},{"text":"Instrumental activities of daily living"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Upper-limb function"},{"text":"Hand function"},{"text":"Cognition"},{"text":"Sensory processing"},{"text":"Work-related function"},{"text":"Home participation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Activities of Daily Living"},{"type":"p","text":"Examples include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Eating"},{"text":"Dressing"},{"text":"Grooming"},{"text":"Bathing"},{"text":"Toileting"},{"text":"Transfers"},{"text":"Mobility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Instrumental activities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cooking"},{"text":"Shopping"},{"text":"Money management"},{"text":"Medication management"},{"text":"Household activities"},{"text":"Community mobility"},{"text":"The goal is to understand how a condition affects real-life function, not just physical symptoms."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Specialized Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop expertise in one or more areas."},{"type":"h","text":"Neurological rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stroke rehabilitation"},{"text":"Brain injury"},{"text":"Spinal cord injury"},{"text":"Parkinson's disease"},{"text":"Multiple sclerosis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motor recovery"},{"text":"Functional retraining"},{"text":"Cognitive rehabilitation"},{"text":"Upper-limb rehabilitation"},{"text":"Adaptive strategies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Orthopedic rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hand rehabilitation"},{"text":"Fracture recovery"},{"text":"Joint replacement"},{"text":"Arthritis"},{"text":"Tendon injuries"},{"text":"Post-surgical rehabilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Pediatric rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Development"},{"text":"Sensory processing"},{"text":"Fine-motor development"},{"text":"School participation"},{"text":"Play"},{"text":"Self-care"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mental-health rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Functional participation"},{"text":"Routine development"},{"text":"Social participation"},{"text":"Vocational rehabilitation"},{"text":"Community reintegration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop competency in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient history"},{"text":"Occupational profile"},{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Physical assessment"},{"text":"Cognitive assessment"},{"text":"Sensory assessment"},{"text":"Environmental assessment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Interview","Occupational Profile","Functional Assessment","Identify Barriers","Set Goals","Treatment Plan","Intervention","Outcome Measurement","Reassessment"]},{"type":"h","text":"Rehabilitation Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to create SMART rehabilitation goals:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Specific"},{"text":"Measurable"},{"text":"Achievable"},{"text":"Relevant"},{"text":"Time-bound"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Instead of:"},{"type":"p","text":"“Improve hand function.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"p","text":"“Improve the patient's ability to independently perform selected dressing tasks using the affected upper limb within the defined rehabilitation period.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Goals should be individualized to the person's functional needs."},{"type":"h","text":"Therapeutic Interventions"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on assessment, training and scope of practice, develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Therapeutic activities"},{"text":"Functional training"},{"text":"Range-of-motion exercises"},{"text":"Strengthening activities"},{"text":"Fine-motor training"},{"text":"Hand therapy"},{"text":"Sensory-based interventions"},{"text":"Cognitive rehabilitation"},{"text":"ADL training"},{"text":"Adaptive techniques"},{"text":"Splinting concepts"},{"text":"Assistive-device training"},{"text":"The specific intervention should always be based on assessment, professional scope and clinical protocols."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Assistive Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wheelchairs"},{"text":"Walking aids"},{"text":"Adaptive eating equipment"},{"text":"Dressing aids"},{"text":"Communication aids"},{"text":"Bathroom modifications"},{"text":"Seating systems"},{"text":"Hand splints"},{"text":"Positioning equipment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to match:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient need","Functional limitation","Assistive solution"]},{"type":"h","text":"Home & Environmental Modification"},{"type":"p","text":"A rehabilitation therapist should understand how the environment affects independence."},{"type":"p","text":"Assess:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Doorways"},{"text":"Stairs"},{"text":"Bathroom safety"},{"text":"Kitchen accessibility"},{"text":"Bed height"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Furniture arrangement"},{"text":"Fall risks"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Functional Limitation","Environmental Assessment","Barrier Identification","Adaptive Equipment / Modification","Training","Improved Independence"]},{"type":"h","text":"Cognitive Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"For neurological rehabilitation, understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Executive function"},{"text":"Problem solving"},{"text":"Orientation"},{"text":"Cognitive strategies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop interventions that support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Daily routines"},{"text":"Medication management"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Work participation"},{"text":"Community independence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Pediatric Occupational Therapy"},{"type":"p","text":"For pediatric rehabilitation, develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental milestones"},{"text":"Fine-motor development"},{"text":"Sensory processing"},{"text":"Handwriting"},{"text":"Self-care"},{"text":"Play"},{"text":"School participation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Work collaboratively with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parents"},{"text":"Teachers"},{"text":"Psychologists"},{"text":"Speech therapists"},{"text":"Physiotherapists"},{"text":"Pediatricians"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mental & Psychosocial Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mental-health conditions"},{"text":"Social participation"},{"text":"Vocational rehabilitation"},{"text":"Community integration"},{"text":"Routine management"},{"text":"Meaningful occupation"},{"text":"The focus is on improving function and participation, not independently providing services outside the therapist's professional scope."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology & Digital Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern rehabilitation increasingly uses technology."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn about:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electronic health records"},{"text":"Tele-rehabilitation"},{"text":"Digital assessment tools"},{"text":"Wearable sensors"},{"text":"Motion tracking"},{"text":"Virtual reality"},{"text":"Robotic rehabilitation"},{"text":"Assistive technology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Use Excel/Power BI for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Functional assessment scores"},{"text":"Therapy attendance"},{"text":"Outcome tracking"},{"text":"Goal achievement"},{"text":"Patient progress"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI in Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore responsible applications of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motion analysis"},{"text":"Personalized rehabilitation plans"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Assistive technology"},{"text":"Progress prediction"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"Virtual rehabilitation"},{"text":"Adaptive therapy systems"},{"text":"AI should support clinical decision-making and outcome measurement rather than replace professional assessment."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project Ideas"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Stroke Rehabilitation Program"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a structured OT program targeting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Upper-limb function"},{"text":"ADLs"},{"text":"Cognitive function"},{"text":"Community participation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Assistive Device Evaluation"},{"type":"p","text":"Evaluate an assistive device based on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"Function"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Independence"},{"text":"Patient satisfaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Home Modification Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop a home-safety assessment framework for individuals with mobility or neurological limitations."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Pediatric OT Intervention"},{"type":"p","text":"Study the effect of a structured activity-based intervention on selected functional skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — End-to-End Rehabilitation Case"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Assessment","Occupational Profile","Functional Limitations","Goal Setting","Intervention Plan","Assistive Technology","Home / Community Strategy","Outcome Measurement","Reassessment"]},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates the complete occupational-therapy reasoning process."},{"type":"h","text":"Internship & Clinical Training Strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize clinical rotations in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rehabilitation hospitals"},{"text":"Neurology rehabilitation"},{"text":"Orthopedic rehabilitation"},{"text":"Pediatric rehabilitation"},{"text":"Hand therapy"},{"text":"Community rehabilitation"},{"text":"Mental-health rehabilitation"},{"text":"Geriatric rehabilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Multidisciplinary exposure"},{"type":"p","text":"Work alongside:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physiotherapists"},{"text":"Speech-language therapists"},{"text":"Psychologists"},{"text":"Nurses"},{"text":"Physicians"},{"text":"Prosthetics and orthotics professionals"},{"text":"Rehabilitation counselors"},{"text":"Understanding the difference between disciplines is essential for effective rehabilitation teamwork."}]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant roles include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Occupational Therapy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Occupational Therapist"},{"text":"Rehabilitation Therapist"},{"text":"Junior Occupational Therapist"},{"text":"Clinical Occupational Therapist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialized rehabilitation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neuro Rehabilitation Therapist"},{"text":"Pediatric Occupational Therapist"},{"text":"Hand Rehabilitation Therapist"},{"text":"Geriatric Rehabilitation Therapist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Community"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Community Rehabilitation Therapist"},{"text":"Home Rehabilitation Therapist"},{"text":"Vocational Rehabilitation Associate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer Requirement","Preparation"],"rows":[[{"text":"BOT"},{"text":"Core qualification"}],[{"text":"Clinical training"},{"text":"Essential"}],[{"text":"Occupational assessment"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Functional rehabilitation"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"ADL training"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Neurological rehabilitation"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Orthopedic rehabilitation"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Pediatric OT"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Assistive technology"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Interdisciplinary teamwork"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Outcome measurement"},{"text":"Strong"}],[{"text":"Digital health"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Intermediate–Strong"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful additional learning areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic Life Support"},{"text":"Neurological rehabilitation"},{"text":"Pediatric occupational therapy"},{"text":"Hand therapy"},{"text":"Assistive technology"},{"text":"Splinting"},{"text":"Cognitive rehabilitation"},{"text":"Sensory integration approaches"},{"text":"Geriatric rehabilitation"},{"text":"Community-based rehabilitation"},{"text":"Tele-rehabilitation"},{"text":"Additional certifications should complement formal OT education and supervised clinical practice."}]}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A postgraduate degree can provide deeper specialization."},{"type":"h","text":"Master of Occupational Therapy / M.Occupational Therapy"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neuro rehabilitation"},{"text":"Hand and upper-limb rehabilitation"},{"text":"Pediatrics"},{"text":"Mental health"},{"text":"Community rehabilitation"},{"text":"Orthopedics"},{"text":"Geriatrics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other pathways"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the institution:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rehabilitation Sciences"},{"text":"Public Health"},{"text":"Healthcare Management"},{"text":"Disability Studies"},{"text":"Assistive Technology"},{"text":"A specialization in neuro, pediatric, hand or community rehabilitation can create a strong clinical identity."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"}]},{"heading":"Neurological Rehabilitation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stroke"},{"text":"Brain injury"},{"text":"Spinal cord injury"},{"text":"Parkinson's disease"}]}]},{"heading":"Pediatric Rehabilitation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Development"},{"text":"School participation"},{"text":"Fine motor skills"},{"text":"Sensory and functional abilities"}]}]},{"heading":"Hand Rehabilitation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hand injuries"},{"text":"Tendon injuries"},{"text":"Fractures"},{"text":"Upper-limb function"}]}]},{"heading":"Geriatric Rehabilitation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Falls"},{"text":"Functional independence"},{"text":"Dementia-related functional needs"},{"text":"Aging-related disability"}]}]},{"heading":"Community Rehabilitation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Home-based care"},{"text":"Community participation"},{"text":"Assistive technology"},{"text":"Vocational reintegration"}]}]},{"heading":"Assistive Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Adaptive equipment"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Environmental modification"},{"text":"Technology-assisted independence"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BOT","Occupational Therapist","Rehabilitation Therapist","Senior Occupational Therapist","Clinical Specialist","Rehabilitation Coordinator","Department / Program Lead","Rehabilitation Services Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"Specialist pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BOT","Clinical Experience","Specialized Rehabilitation Training","Specialist Occupational Therapist","Advanced Clinical Practice","Clinical / Rehabilitation Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"Academic/research pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BOT","Clinical Experience","Master's in Occupational Therapy / Related Field","Research / Teaching","Senior Academic / Research Role","Rehabilitation Research Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"The rehabilitation sector is increasingly adopting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Virtual reality"},{"text":"Augmented reality"},{"text":"Robotic rehabilitation"},{"text":"Wearable sensors"},{"text":"Motion capture"},{"text":"Computer-vision assessment"},{"text":"Tele-rehabilitation"},{"text":"AI-assisted movement analysis"},{"text":"Smart assistive devices"},{"text":"3D-printed adaptive equipment"},{"text":"Digital therapeutics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The future rehabilitation professional will increasingly combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Clinical OT","Assistive Technology","Data","Digital Rehabilitation."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Occupational therapy"},{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Rehabilitation science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rehabilitation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ADL training"},{"text":"Neurological rehabilitation"},{"text":"Orthopedic rehabilitation"},{"text":"Pediatric rehabilitation"},{"text":"Cognitive rehabilitation"},{"text":"Geriatric rehabilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Assistive Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Adaptive equipment"},{"text":"Wheelchairs"},{"text":"Splinting"},{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Home modification"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EHR"},{"text":"Tele-rehabilitation"},{"text":"Wearable technology"},{"text":"VR/AR"},{"text":"Motion analysis"},{"text":"Basic data analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Caregiver education"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"},{"text":"Interdisciplinary teamwork"},{"text":"Goal setting"},{"text":"Outcome measurement"},{"text":"Ethical practice"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"flow","items":["BOT","Biomedical Foundation","Occupational Therapy Fundamentals","Functional Assessment","ADL + Rehabilitation Skills","Neuro / Ortho / Pediatric Exposure","Assistive Technology","Clinical Internship","Outcome Measurement","Multidisciplinary Rehabilitation Experience","Rehabilitation Therapist Readiness"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"For BOT → Occupational Therapy → Rehabilitation Therapist, the strongest candidate is a function-focused rehabilitation professional who can assess how illness or disability affects everyday activities and then design evidence-based interventions that improve independence and participation."},{"type":"p","text":"The highest-value combination is functional assessment + ADL rehabilitation + neurological/orthopedic knowledge + assistive technology + patient/caregiver education + outcome measurement. With experience and postgraduate specialization, the pathway can progress toward clinical specialization, rehabilitation coordination, academic roles, research, or rehabilitation-service leadership."}]}]}